---
title: Diced vegetable soup
description: Lesson 7.4. The module together. Every cut in one pot, and why they should match.
servings: 4
time: 50 minutes
tags: [cooking-course, mastering-the-knife]
lesson: "7.4"
technique: dicing to a size
status: draft
---

> Technique: cutting to a size. This soup uses every cut in the
> module: the onion dice from lesson 7.1, the mince from 7.2, the
> planks and sticks from 7.3. The only new thing is the target: every
> piece 1 cm across.

Dice @onion{1} as in lesson 7.1, with the cuts 1 cm apart.

Peel @carrots{2} and cut them into 5 cm lengths. Take a thin slice off one side so each sits flat, cut it into planks 1 cm thick, the planks into sticks 1 cm wide, and the sticks across into dice. Do the same with @celery{2%sticks} and @potato{250%g}(peeled).

> Why the same size: the aim of dicing is even pieces that cook at the
> same rate. If the carrot is twice the size of the potato, one is
> hard when the other is falling apart.
-- source: Liz Bomze, "A Guide to Using Your Chef's Knife", America's Test Kitchen, 2018-12-05, https://www.americastestkitchen.com/articles/1362-a-guide-to-using-your-chef-s-knife ; Keith Dresser, "How to Cut Carrots", America's Test Kitchen, 2021-06-07, https://www.americastestkitchen.com/articles/3368-how-to-cut-carrots

Mince @garlic{2%cloves} and finely chop @parsley{2%tbsp}.

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large pot{} over medium-low heat. Add the onion, carrot and celery with a pinch of salt and cook for ~{10%minutes}, stirring now and then, until soft and not coloured.

Add the garlic and stir for ~{1%minute}, no longer.

> Why the garlic goes in late: minced garlic burns easily and turns
> acrid and bitter: its sugar starts to brown and then scorches as
> soon as it gets hot. Add it when the other vegetables
> are nearly soft and give it 30 to 60 seconds before the liquid goes
> in.
-- source: Liz Bomze, "Wait! Don't Add Your Garlic Just Yet", America's Test Kitchen, 2023-09-14, https://www.americastestkitchen.com/articles/7557-why-you-should-wait-to-add-garlic

Add the potato and @vegetable stock{1%litre}. Bring to a boil, then simmer for ~{15%minutes}, until a piece of potato and a piece of carrot are both tender. Taste, add @salt{1/2%tsp} a pinch at a time, and stir in the parsley.

> If it goes wrong: if some pieces are soft and others hard, the dice
> was uneven. Look at what is left on your board next time: the
> pieces should look like they came from the same vegetable.

> Next time, without the recipe: pick the size first, then make every
> cut to it. Planks, sticks, dice, in that order, for anything.
